{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA → 48.5% acc), which provides a weak baseline and leaves the most critical question for a multimodal study unanswered: does image data carry a stronger or complementary signal? Testing config_010 (image-only, single-profile, ResNet50) establishes the image modality's standalone performance under the same profile setting as config_001, giving us a clean unimodal comparison. This is essential before evaluating any multimodal fusion configuration, because without knowing each modality's ceiling we cannot attribute gains (or losses) to fusion versus to a stronger single modality. If image alone substantially outperforms RNA, it reshapes the entire search toward image-centric or fusion-weighted configurations; if it is comparable, it motivates testing whether multimodal combination adds value. Under a tight budget, this single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design axis (modality contribution) and directly informs the next 2–3 experiments."
}

